    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>16</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>In a Harvard-style CPU, there would
be actual instruction memory here.
Instead, we have a tunnel to our
memory block and a tunnel back.

This is a good compromise for us.
However, another option is doing
a fetch/execute design, where
we spend a clock cycle getting the
instruction and then another using it.
(Or, of course, we could pipeline
this processor.)</string>
        </entry>
